# netconnect pins registry — which container each DB entrypoint is pinned to.
# One line per pin:   <entrypoint>=<container-name>     e.g.  postgres=pg-primary
#
# This file only tells the sidecar to KEEP the pinned container attached. The
# actual deterministic routing is done by a generated dynamic/pin-<ep>.yaml
# (high-priority Traefik file router). Both are written by `make pin` and removed
# by `make unpin` — edit by hand only if you know why, then `make restart`.
# No pins here == plain reject-extras (first claimant of a port wins).
#
# This .example is the versioned template. The live pins.conf is per-machine
# (references local container names) and is gitignored; `make init`/`make up`
# seed it from this file, and `make pin`/`make unpin` maintain it.
